<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Polish–Swedish War (1626–1629)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1626">1626</a>–<a href="/years/1629">1629</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Polish–Swedish War of 1626–1629 was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustavus-adolphus">Gustavus Adolphus</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish–Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>, chiefly in Royal and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duchy-of-prussia">Ducal Prussia</a>. Despite a Polish naval victory at Oliwa (1627) and Koniecpolski's win at Trzciana (1629), the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/truce-of-altmark">Truce of Altmark</a> (1629) left Sweden most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonia">Livonia</a> and the toll revenues of Prussian ports, freeing it to enter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/polish-swedish-war-1626-1629.jpg" alt="Polish–Swedish War (1626–1629)" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Józef Brandt · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bitwa_pod_Trzcian%C4%85.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
